-- A default naming something that is not in scope is reported once, as that:
-- `zzz` is not defined. It used to be reported a second time as "must be a
-- literal", which was a misleading way to say it (p10 of
-- TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md), on a rule's input and on a record's field.

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY zzz
GIVETH A NUMBER
f MEANS x

DECLARE Gauge HAS
  level IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY yyy
